// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 15-function-semantics
// facility: rule.fn.closure spec/14 deriv (CHG-0100); conf.closure-capture-written-while-held-rejected
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// A closure without `move` borrows each capture for as long as it
// exists, exclusively when its body writes it (spec/15 §6). Writing
// `count` while `bump` holds it faulted only when run; a binding holding
// such a closure now carries spec/14's `deriv` facts, as a spawn's
// handle does, and the write is refuted statically. Found by real-world
// testing (a batch of common borrow mistakes).

import std;

fn main()
{
    i32 count = 0;
    auto bump = [count]() : void { count += 1; };
    count = 10;
    bump();
}
